oject  with the the school of business and  economics that you know helped them uh  get you know  get through their uh re-accreditation i  got involved in the entire  reaccreditation thing and helped write  the 10-year quality enhancement plan uh  one entire chapter is is what i wrote  and i had a part in the others i  defended the the plan to uh sacks which  is the uh the reaccreditors i  was involved in and then ran  university-wide  assessment of student learning so i was  you know i was getting pretty uh well  positioned there but something else  happened that changed their trajectory  of where i was going  entirely  and led to me moving somewhere else  the next stop for me was to move up to  new york and into the hudson valley  specifically to kingston which is on the  west side of the the river  and i started teaching for a place on  the east side of the river called marist  college and i started teaching as an  adjunct now why would i leave  a position where i had job security i  was involved in all these different  things i was actually up for  early tenure and early promotion if i  had  stayed well because i fell in love and  it was with somebody who i knew from  high school i think many of you know  this story andy shaka and i went to  catholic memorial high school together  uh we met when when i was a sophomore  and she was a freshman she actually  dated a guy who was at that time my  archrival  and then you know we we lose track of  each other we cross paths again living  here in milwaukee in the 1990s both of  us working at a building just blocks  from here called the hundred east  building  and um you know flirted with each other  didn't really recognize who each other  were saw each other constantly then we  lose track of each other again  and then it is uh late 2009  and she keeps popping up on facebook as  a hey maybe you should a friend request  this person so i do  and then we start talking and within  a month  we have and by talking i mean writing to  each other this is before we even talked  on the phone we fall in love we decide  we're going to get married we start  thinking about plans  we begin talking on the phone and  by summer i have gone up there and you  know we have  met each other face to face again for  the first time in you know decades uh we  go to a conference in toronto together  and start doing all sorts of things then  we begin the long distance  part of our relationship where i would  fly from fayetteville not actually  flying village to drive up to raleigh  and then take a plane from there to jfk  in new york city and then she would  drive down and pick me up and we'd drive  up to the hudson valley and we'd have 48  hours together and then drive back down  and do the whole thing all over again  and after a while that got kind of old  and we're like listen you know we're in  our 40s  screw this long distance stuff you're  not coming down to the south this this  place is messed up i'll go up there by  you  and she had a you know solid gig as a  a assistant dean at the culinary  institute of america she founded the  center for excellence in teaching and  learning you can tell she's a real  go-getter right so um  she had taught at marist college  previously and she said why don't you uh  why don't you adjunct at marist college  you know it's a decent place to go  so i started doing that and i started  teaching intro to philosophy and ethics  for them eventually i taught you know  religion in american culture and you've  you've probably seen those videos from  my early classes  and i did apply for full-time positions  in various places but by then the job  market had really dried up you know  we're still not out of the financial  crisis in 2011 when when i moved up  there  and um you know i i just kept teaching  for for marist eventually i transitioned  actually very early on my second  semester there i start teaching online  for them  because i could take my videos and the  very rich  resources that i provided in my course  management system i begin teaching  online  and you know i start doing all sorts of  other things i get involved in  educational startups obviously i spend a  lot of time shooting youtube videos i  begin building my own business reason i  owe while i'm there originally so that i  can get  i can get tax write-offs for public  speaking and then i start tutoring and  then i get um you know philosophical uh  counseling certification and training  and i begin doing that and i start doing  consulting for businesses and so  you know that went on for quite a while  we were there from 2011  to  2015  and then uh andy's job changed and she  became a consultant rather than an  employee of the culinary institute of  america which meant  that we could now  move back here  to milwaukee  we didn't have to be there in new york  anymore  and we were like yeah let's let's come  home  so you know with our two dogs and kat  and our you know  who knows how many books we had we had  99 bankers boxes worth of books  we prepared for  moving out now i continued teaching  for marist though i kept that because i  was teaching  online  and by that time i was teaching a  different class which i i've actually  replicated in my teachable  study with sadler academy called world  views and values which is sort of like a  an introduction to philosophy class  except it's got some other twists to it  as well  so we reached the final chapter in this  long story the milwaukee years which i'm  still in at present  and when i first got back here i was  still teaching for marist college uh  generally one class per  semester and i was you know  shooting youtube videos i began  podcasting i was working uh on some you  know educational startup stuff and i was  working  uh with with businesses as well starting  to do executive coaching and um you know  other things along those lines ethics  consulting  doing a lot of tutorial work as well so  i you know i had my marist sideline and  then i had my my business stuff over  here  and then the  first  uh main place that i started teaching  for and i believe this was in  2017 in the fall semester was marquette  university  and the way that ended up happening was  i i had done some presentations at  marquette for the philosophy department  and my friend owen over there  he  said hey we've got a visiting assistant  professor position why don't you uh  interview for it and i did and in the  interview i found out that they were  paying essentially peanuts and the  interview basically was over at that  point because i was like uh no they also  had a non-compete clause i'd have to  close down my tutorials not teach for  anyone else and i was like you can't  live on that here in the city with what  you're offering and so that be i was  like that that's that for marquette and  then within like a week they emailed me  and said um  do you think you could teach as an  adjunct for us we've got these ethics  classes  and  the provost is playing around with class  sizes and shrinking them so we now have  a lot more sections that we have to fill  do you think you could help us out and i  was like yeah yeah that'd be great so i  start you know walking to marquette in  the  mornings two days a week and teaching  over there and i've got an office that  i'm sharing with the other adjuncts most  of whom are graduate students and so  it's kind of fun to be like in a  university again you know not not just a  college but a real university  access the library all that kind of  stuff so i'm teaching at marquette and  that was like a pretty reliable  continuing gig and they paid pretty well  for for adjunct teaching  and then i got  solicited by carthage college down in  kenosha wanting to know if i could teach  some philosophy classes for them  particularly business ethics which i was  also teaching at marquette and i was  like yeah i like teaching business  ethics i think it's actually really  important so i begin teaching one class  a semester down there  at carthage as well you notice what's  going on by that time marist becomes  unreliable and it's also messing up our  taxes because it winds up having to pay  you know wisconsin tax and new york tax  so we're like  we're done with marist so now i've got a  couple places i'm teaching i also  apply at milwaukee  area technical college in part because  people are like oh man that's a really  great gig you know if you get in there  pays well you know it's reliable as it  turned out that was true 10 years before  but they'd like a lot of places where  people  took too many liberties then they  clamped down and everything became very  bureaucratic  that was the most dysfunctional place  i've ever taught for there was no  onboarding they have all these crazy  practices and processes the website was  a total mess and unhelpful  people would just like you know  the schedules are just like schedule you  for classes without consulting you it  didn't pay well but i taught there for  for a  a number of semesters  and then i also taught i began teaching  in 2018 for milwaukee  institute of art and design so by this  time i got lots of teaching as a matter  of fact i'm turning down classes  because i'm you know a reliable teacher  and and uh they need the the people to  teach these classes and so i'm teaching  like you know one class here or two  classes here and they're asking me can  you do more for us  and  you know the only the only  one i didn't turn down classes for was  milwaukee institute of art and design  because i really really liked working  there  but you know carthage began kind of  souring on me  same thing with milwaukee area technical  college as a matter of fact they didn't  even begin they started sour  and you know marquette um  it was okay you know and then covet hit  right  so with marquette that meant that  enrollment went down and a lot of things  dried up  i did teach  two sections in  2020 of  business ethics online and that was the  last that i taught for marquette  milwaukee area technical college was  already a mess and cove had made them  even more of a mess  but i kept teaching for them i also  taught prison students for them i should  mention um you know  in the second chance pell program but  then i left that because it was it was  so badly managed as well  um it's too bad because i thought it was  a great program it's just it was poorly  put together and poorly managed  so  you know i started pairing things away  you know marquette went away carthage  wanted me to teach more for them they  they would have had me i did teach two  classes one semester for them online  and during the pandemic they were all  about going online and then as soon as  they thought it was safe they wanted  everything to go away from online and i  was like listen i'm i'm  i'm high risk my wife is even higher  risk i'm not going down to campus to  teach  classes for you all i'm happy to teach  online if you want me to and that  continued all the way to the end of this  this last academic year  and so i started you know marquette went  away carthage  the the writing was on the wall they  also eliminated their philosophy program  and so i was there basically to help  them finish out the majors and i i  decided to quit teaching for milwaukee  area technical college so now i've just  got the one gig as of the end of this  this  spring semester i've only got the one  gig teaching for milwaukee institute of  art and design quite happy with that  because not teaching as many classes as  an adjunct for these other places means  i can concentrate on other things like  my study with sadler academy or light  hall platform classes or listenable  classes or you know being  continuing my client work in tutorials  philosophical counseling ethics  consulting and all these other things as  well so that is the story and this spans  you know more than  20 years starting down in carbondale  illinois finishing up here in milwaukee  a whole bunch of different universities  colleges on the way that i have taught  for  and now you got the whole scoop up to  today things could change in semesters  to come but you know now you know where  i've been what i've done who i've taught  for  why i quit teaching for them why i moved  on to other things you got the full  story  you
 

